{"content":[{"c":["EUNUCH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Officer or chamberlain in the court or household of a ruler, often assigned to the women’s quarters. Many of these men were emasculated, though not always (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.39.1","r":"Gen.39.1","rawR":"Gen.39.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.39.1","value":"Gen.39.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 39:1"},", ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Eunuchs were public officials in Israel (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.8.15","r":"1Sam.8.15","rawR":"1Sam.8.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.8.15","value":"1Sam.8.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 8:15"},", ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.28.1","r":"1Chr.28.1","rawR":"1Chr.28.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.28.1","value":"1Chr.28.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 28:1"},", ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), Persia (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.2.3","r":"Esth.2.3","rawR":"Esth.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.2.3","value":"Esth.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 2:3"},"), Ethiopia (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.38.7","r":"Jer.38.7","rawR":"Jer.38.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.38.7","value":"Jer.38.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 38:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.8.27","r":"Acts.8.27","rawR":"Acts.8.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.8.27","value":"Acts.8.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 8:27"},"), and Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Dan.1.3","r":"Dan.1.3","rawR":"Dan.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.1.3","value":"Dan.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dn 1:3"},"). Eunuchs were not included in public worship in Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.23.1","r":"Deut.23.1","rawR":"Deut.23.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.23.1","value":"Deut.23.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 23:1"},"), but the prophet Isaiah referred to their restoration in the messianic kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.56.3-5","r":"Isa.56.3-5","rawR":"Isa.56.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.56.3-5","value":"Isa.56.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 56:3-5"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.8.1-40","r":"Acts.8.1-40","rawR":"Acts.8.1-40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.8.1-40","value":"Acts.8.1-40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 8"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The Ethiopian eunuch of ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.8.27-39","r":"Acts.8.27-39","rawR":"Acts.8.27-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.8.27-39","value":"Acts.8.27-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 8:27-39"}," was probably minister of the treasury and has been credited with founding Christianity in Ethiopia."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Jesus mentioned three classes of eunuchs (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.19.12","r":"Matt.19.12","rawR":"Matt.19.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.19.12","value":"Matt.19.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 19:12"},"), including those who made themselves eunuchs for the sake of the kingdom. This is generally understood in a metaphorical sense of voluntarily forgoing marriage in order to serve the kingdom (e.g., John the Baptist, Jesus, and the apostle Paul)."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eunuch","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 39:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.39.1","rawQueryValue":"Gen.39.1","sourceRefExact":"Gen.39.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 8:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.8.15","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.8.15","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.8.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 28:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.28.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.28.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.28.1"},{"anchorText":"Est 2:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Esth.2.3","rawQueryValue":"Esth.2.3","sourceRefExact":"Esth.2.3"},{"anchorText":"Jer 38:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.38.7","rawQueryValue":"Jer.38.7","sourceRefExact":"Jer.38.7"},{"anchorText":"Acts 8:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.8.27","rawQueryValue":"Acts.8.27","sourceRefExact":"Acts.8.27"},{"anchorText":"Dn 1:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Dan.1.3","rawQueryValue":"Dan.1.3","sourceRefExact":"Dan.1.3"},{"anchorText":"Dt 23:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.23.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.23.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.23.1"},{"anchorText":"Is 56:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.56.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Isa.56.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Isa.56.3-5"},{"anchorText":"Acts 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.8.1-40","rawQueryValue":"Acts.8.1-40","sourceRefExact":"Acts.8.1-40"},{"anchorText":"Acts 8:27-39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.8.27-39","rawQueryValue":"Acts.8.27-39","sourceRefExact":"Acts.8.27-39"},{"anchorText":"Mt 19:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.19.12","rawQueryValue":"Matt.19.12","sourceRefExact":"Matt.19.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f2e98f502375eb0b08f4761a6caf8862c9041913ca874f0be614779e539a1f70","sourceItemName":"Eunuch","sourceItemOrder":273,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Eunuch","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Eunuch","title":"Eunuch","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}